      "content": "That's getting closer to the style I like. The \"symphony\" and \"sanctuary\" bit is nice. \n\nI just checked the tool again and it's still flagging the paragraph as \"moderately descriptive.\" For my main feature piece, I usually try to hit that \"highly rich\" tier so the prose really pops on the page. \n\nCould you give it one more pass? Really dial up the descriptive elements—the scents, the lighting effects, the textures of the food—to maximize that richness score. I'm still really worried about it looking fake though, so please try to make sure the adjectives actually belong there and aren't just being thrown in for the sake of the count. I want the reader to feel like they are actually sitting in the bistro.",
